Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. CONTRACTOR WORKROOM - SUNDAY MORNING

Voss places two transport files side by side. Vale recognises the child before he gives the historic identifier.

VALE
Yellow coat.

The first file: WESTMERE. Temporary placement. Maternal contact continuing. A review ahead.

MEMORY — A SERVICE STATION, YEARS EARLIER

A girl shivers in a coat too thin for the weather. Reyes puts his own coat around her. A paper cup disappears between oversized sleeves.

REYES
Your teeth are doing the paperwork for you.

BACK IN THE WORKROOM

Vale touches a line: REQUESTED MOTHER REPEATEDLY.

VOSS
Real authority. That journey.

Eleven weeks later: MERIDIAN. Contact suspended. Private receiving household. A different order.

Dispatch Friday. Authority Monday. Voss puts a finger on ACTIVATION PENDING AUTHORITY.

VALE
The house was waiting.

VOSS
A destination before an order can be legitimate. We prove what this one did.

Property-service records: child-specific clothes and a room prepared forty-eight hours before the disputed authority. A premium tied to avoiding external escalation. Meridian's contractor onboarding, supported by AC019.

A dispatcher answers on speaker. Jobs were released when the attached authority arrived; somebody else was assumed to have checked the client.

Voss opens his own debrief. CHILD RESISTANT AT INITIAL CONTACT.

MEMORY — A TEMPORARY CARER'S HALLWAY

The girl stands behind the carer. Voss holds out the order. Vale waits by the door.

CARER
Her mother's finished treatment. There's a review coming.

Voss indicates the verification number printed on the document. The carer calls. Listens. Returns the order, her certainty gone.

GIRL
Does Mum know?

VOSS
It's arranged.

BACK IN THE WORKROOM

Voss does not look away from the line he wrote years ago.

VOSS
I didn't know that.

He types what he remembers: the challenge, the supplied number, the confirmation, his answer to the child. Separates it from what the retained records establish.

VALE
She did everything right.

VOSS
And we treated the answer as enough.

Vale reaches towards the search field. Stops before entering the girl's name.

VALE
She'd be grown now.

VOSS
We don't need her current life to prove our job.

She closes the search. They preserve the two files together.

INT. GUESTHOUSE - SUNDAY EVENING

Zoe reads their bounded account through the relay. The drive stays closed.

ZOE
Someone knew the household. Someone supplied the order. He told her it was arranged.

ELIAS
He says he did.

ZOE
At least he put himself in it.

She writes one sentence, then puts down the notebook. Elias checks the lock.

ZOE
Tomorrow?

ELIAS
North Vale may ask Westmere directly.

ZOE
Good.

The first journey's request for her mother remains beside the second journey's word: RESISTANT.
